      P(2, 'models', 'A therapist says a client’s fear of dogs was learned when a neutral stimulus (dogs) was paired with pain from a bite. Which model and which process?', '<b>Cognitive-behavioral (behavioral) model, classical conditioning.</b> Operant conditioning would involve consequences of the client’s own behavior.'),
      P(3, 'models', 'Name the defense mechanism: after failing an exam, Jo says the test was unfair and she did not care anyway.', '<b>Rationalization</b> (creating an acceptable reason for an unacceptable outcome). Denial would be refusing to accept that she failed at all.'),
      P(4, 'assessment', 'Two clinicians watch the same interview and assign the same diagnosis. What kind of reliability is this?', '<b>Interrater (interjudge) reliability.</b> Test-retest reliability would compare the same test given twice to the same person.'),
      P(5, 'anxiety', 'For eight months, Kim has worried about grades, money, her parents’ health and the weather most days, with muscle tension, fatigue and poor sleep. Diagnosis?', '<b>Generalized anxiety disorder:</b> excessive worry about many things for 6+ months with at least 3 of the 6 symptoms (tension, fatigue, sleep trouble).'),
      P(6, 'anxiety', 'What is the most effective treatment for specific phobias, and what is its principle?', '<b>Exposure</b> (systematic desensitization, flooding or modeling): repeated contact with the feared object without escape lets the fear extinguish.'),
      P(7, 'trauma', 'Five weeks after an assault, a woman has flashbacks, avoids the area, feels detached and startles easily. Acute stress disorder or PTSD?', '<b>PTSD</b>: the symptoms have lasted more than one month. Acute stress disorder covers 3 days to 1 month.'),
      P(8, 'trauma', 'What does research say about psychological debriefing right after a trauma?', 'It has <b>not</b> been shown to prevent PTSD, and some studies suggest it can increase symptoms. Trauma-focused CBT for those who develop symptoms has better support.')
